WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 1 Student Video
Unit 1, Lesson 1: Apologetics

1
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.080
Are there answers to our questions? From

2
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.660
the simplest things that pass through our consciousness to

3
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.070
the big questions about life and faith.

4
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.380
The word apologetics comes from the Greek word apologia, which can be translated as

5
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:49.120
answer. It means to give a reason, a defense, or an answer for what we believe

6
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.420
and why we believe it. When I was in college, I went to a friend's wedding and had

7
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.840
to fly home alone. I got to the airport in the morning and learned that my flight

8
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.680
was delayed about three or four hours so I turned around to go wait and I

9
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.860
saw another young man about my age he was in college and I thought you know what

10
00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:14.800
here's an opportunity to go talk with him and maybe share my faith but then my

11
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:20.480
next thought was you know what I am really tired God if you want me to share with

12
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.400
him he's gonna have to sit by me on the plane I finally boarded the plane and I

13
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.660
sat down in seat 9A. A few moments later, I saw this young man walking down the

14
00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.920
aisle and of course I'm wondering where he's gonna sit and he sits right next to me

15
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:40.820
in 9B. Whether this was a sign from God or not, it certainly was an opportunity

16
00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.780
so I introduced myself, struck up a conversation and eventually the topic turned

17
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.380
towards spiritual things. He asked me what I believe.

18
00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.400
I said, I'm a Christian, I believe in Jesus.

19
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.680
He said, if you're a Christian, Does that mean you think that the Bible is true and

20
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.880
it's the Word of God? I said, yes.

21
00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.540
He looked at me point blank. I'll never forget it.

22
00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.100
He said, how do you really know the Bible's true?

23
00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.980
And although my parents had trained me to give an answer, for some reason in this

24
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.440
circumstance, I fumbled around. And to be honest with you, I gave an answer that was

25
00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:13.560
really weak.

26
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.880
I walked away from that encounter a little bit upset and frustrated that I didn't

27
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.340
have a better response. And I remember thinking, next time, I'm going to have a

28
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.920
better answer. In fact, I remember having a resolve that said, if God gives me the

29
00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.740
chance to be in significant spiritual conversations again, I'm going to have a good

30
00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.460
reason for why I believe in Christianity and specifically why I think the Bible is

31
00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:37.700
true.

32
00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:44.400
In 1 Peter 3:15, the Apostle Peter says to put Christ first in our

33
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.420
life, but then to be ready with an answer for the hope within and to give it with

34
00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:52.880
gentleness and to give it with respect towards other people.

35
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.180
What's fascinating to me about this passage is the pattern in which Peter says to

36
00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.600
first make Christ Lord of your life, and then be ready with an answer.

37
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.660
Sometimes we flip this around. Sometimes we want to be ready with an answer before

38
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.540
we've really submitted our lives to Christ.

39
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.380
And when that happens, oftentimes the results can be harmful.

40
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.660
But when we first find our identity in Christ and we experience his forgiveness and

41
00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:27.300
then we do apologetics out of a spirit of love, it can make a powerful difference in

42
00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:27.940
somebody's life.

43
00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:34.660
Being an apologist is not a spiritual gift like wisdom, discernment or teaching.

44
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.500
Being an apologist is not just for pastors, teachers, parents and professors.

45
00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:44.460
We are all called to be ready with an answer for the hope within.

46
00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:50.200
I think C.S. Lewis is right. The question is not if we will be apologists, but how

47
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.060
good of an apologist will each of us be?

48
00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.440
Apologetics has been a staple of the Christian faith since its inception.

49
00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:03.380
Jesus was a kind of apologist and the first followers of Jesus that came after the

50
00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:08.860
apostles, many of them were called apologists because they gave positive evidences

51
00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.600
for the Christian faith and responded to objections against it.

52
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.680
How much have you thought about why you believe as you believe?

53
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.680
Are you ready with an answer when someone asks you why you think the Bible is true?

54
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.640
Have you thought through why if God is all good and all powerful, he allows evil?

55
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.660
And have you thought through a response when people say that science conflicts with

56
00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.460
faith? and just as importantly are you ready to share that answer with others when

57
00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:41.160
they ask you the reason for the hope within we are called as Christians to be

58
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:46.700
ready to make a case for the Christian faith we're called to put forth arguments for

59
00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:51.380
what we believe now don't confuse that with being argumentative that's a very

60
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:56.560
different thing we are not called to be divisive in how we treat people but each of

61
00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.800
us are called to be ready with an answer for the hope within and that's exactly

62
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.500
what we're going to do in this Bible study.

63
00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:07.420
I'm going to help you develop your convictions that Christianity is true and also

64
00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.800
have the confidence to share that faith with others.

65
00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:16.520
And just remember this, we are called to boldly speak truth, but we are to always do

66
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:17.740
it in love.

